<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 2.0 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 2.0 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 1.8 points, 2.0 percent, to 77.35 points after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index lost 39.21 points, 1.13 percent, to 3,429.08.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over the local market was 9.18 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove Index is a capitalisation weighted basket Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
